From cbcef6bde13ac2933400937e001d929ec11e36f4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Longwei Yang <19267252+Longwei-Yang@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 15:51:24 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Safarium: Safari-style animated video full screen

When a page element such as a video goes full screen, move it into its own
full-screen window and zoom it there from its place in the page, live, the
way Safari does; on exit it shrinks back into place while the page keeps a
placeholder (page snapshot plus the video's last frame) until the page has
drawn the video in place again.

- Blink reports the full-screen element's rect (safarium_fullscreen.mojom,
  SafariumFullscreenHost) so the zoom starts and ends at the right spot.
- ExclusiveAccessContext::GetTabFullscreenOverride lets the Safarium window
  handle tab full screen itself.
- ViewsNSWindowDelegate supports AppKit's custom full-screen enter/exit
  animations and destinationWindowToExitFullScreenForWindow, so leaving
  full screen returns to the browser window's Space (desktop or the full
  screen browser) without passing through other Spaces. Only windows that
  ask for it change; NativeWidgetMacNSWindow skips frame constraining for
  them so the video window starts at its final full-screen size.
- The video window is screen-sized from the start and only its compositor
  layer zooms, so the picture stays live (resizing a window during the
  transition freezes it).
- On exit, wait (up to 1.5 s) until the page's videos are back at their
  original size before fading the placeholder; sites such as YouTube resize
  their video with script after full screen ends.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
